meta {
  name: Invite Member
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/company/:id/members
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  id: 3ad4d39f-8a12-491e-8f7b-f0b371861622
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "replace-with-invitee-email"
  }
}

docs {
  Requires JwtAuthGuard + CompanyMemberGuard: the caller must already be a
  member of the company (:id) in the path.

  Contract input is { id, email } — id comes from the :id path param,
  email is the only field to send in the body.

  Service is currently a stub: it does not persist an invitation, generate
  a token, or send an email yet — it just returns a confirmation string.

  Remaining endpoints from MembersController are not implemented yet
  (commented out as TODO in the controller): change member role (PATCH),
  remove member (DELETE), list members (GET).
}
